# Deliberately empty.
#
# Passed to `docker compose --env-file` for the dev database (see
# docker-compose.dev.yml and the db:* scripts in package.json). Docker Compose
# always auto-loads a project's .env for ${VAR} interpolation, and this
# project's .env holds a bcrypt hash full of `$` characters that Compose's
# parser mangles into bogus variable references. Pointing --env-file at this
# empty file instead stops Compose from touching the app's .env at all, which
# docker-compose.dev.yml has no need for anyway — its credentials are fixed
# literals, not pulled from the environment.
